ommitments without the earnings to back them."], [16.033, 17.74, "What buys time is cash."], [18.1, 19.354, "After the IPO,"], [19.4, 21.176, "he expects about $200 billion,"], [21.664, 23.255, "enough to cover the next two or three"], [23.289, 24.462, "years of those bills."], [24.822, 27.481, "But only if revenue roughly doubles every year"], [27.527, 28.409, "in the near term."], [28.897, 31.521, "That's the one number he says drives everything."], [31.95, 33.355, "If revenue comes in,"], [33.436, 34.504, "profits come,"], [34.864, 36.315, "the commitments get paid,"], [36.397, 37.674, "and the risk goes away."], [38.103, 39.021, "If it doesn't,"], [39.218, 40.867, "everything else falls apart."], [41.435, 43.606, "Host Ed Elson pointed out that growth was"], [43.676, 47.53, "already slowing, from 47% a quarter toward 15"], [47.611, 48.738, "to 25%."], [49.132, 51.071, "Damodaran blames competition:"], [51.524, 54.717, "OpenAI underpricing, and cheaper open models."], [55.564, 57.132, "Most businesses don't need Claude,"], [57.178, 57.759, "he says."], [58.281, 59.279, "It's overkill."], [60.115, 62.855, "His advice: build models powerful enough,"], [63.099, 64.261, "but not too powerful."], [64.597, 66.455, "And even if AI helps cure diseases,"], [66.478, 67.175, "he warns,"], [67.662, 69.497, "the value may flow to all of us,"], [70.17, 72.004, "not to Anthropic's shareholders."], [72.678, 74.535, "So why hasn't he written it off?"]]}, "S05": {"frames": 1876, "words": [["Part", 0.0, 0.325], ["five.", 0.395, 0.929], ["Why", 1.358, 1.695], ["he", 1.788, 1.881], ["might", 2.009, 2.276], ["still", 2.322, 2.589], ["buy.", 2.682, 3.216], ["Damodaran", 3.704, 4.284], ["thinks", 4.331, 4.54], ["AI", 4.621, 5.074], ["ends", 5.143, 5.341], ["up", 5.375, 5.445], ["with", 5.492, 5.619], ["two", 5.654, 5.782], ["or", 5.851, 5.921], ["three", 5.956, 6.13], ["big", 6.165, 6.316], ["players,", 6.385, 6.966], ["and", 7.233, 7.407], ["Anthropic,", 7.477, 8.173], ["the", 8.197, 8